               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Instructions for use</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Instructions for use</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Remote control operation man-machine separation, safer and easi</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Remote control operation man-machine separation, safer and easier operation, labor liberation</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Precautions for use</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Precautions for use</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>* Tighten the screws and bolts of each part for each operation.</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>* Tighten the screws and bolts of each part for each operation. Also, make sure there are no loose or missing wires and wiring. please confirm. * Due to the loosening of screws and bolts due to vibration during use, and poor contact, please check in time, otherwise it may cause equipment failure or damage. * If you drive for a long time with only the motor running, the remaining battery power will decrease significantly, and you may not be able to run it because it does not generate electricity. â€¢ To avoid overheating and damage to parts, we recommend that you allow the unit to rest for 10 minutes when refueling. After the equipment is filled with oil, it can work continuously for about 1 hour before refueling. â€¢ Before first use, please charge for 3-6 hours until fully charged. â€¢ Please start up the equipment in the correct sequence to avoid damage to the equipment. â€¢ Before turning on the remote control, please make sure all the buttons on the remote control are in the original state (middle position), otherwise the signal cannot be received normally. â€¢ When adjusting the height of mowing blades and dozer blades, please adjust the relevant operating levers to the appropriate height and then return to the middle position. â€¢ Be sure to use the supplied charger when charging the battery. â€¢ Please replenish the specified amount of gasoline and engine oil before use. Â·Check the condition of gasoline, oil and battery before use after long-term storage. â€¢Do not let the remote control get wet from rain, etc., as it may cause a malfunction. â€¢ When storing, turn off the power switch of the equipment and battery, and remove the mud and dirt attached to the main body, engine, electric control box, etc. Â· Be aware that lack of oil may result in engine damage.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>About the remote</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>About the remote</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>â€¢ The remote uses 4 AA batteries. â€¢ Batteries are not included,</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>â€¢ The remote uses 4 AA batteries. â€¢ Batteries are not included, please prepare separately. â€¢ Since the remote controller has initial settings, please use it directly without any setting (adjustment). â€¢ Normally, "high speed" is used to mow grass. If the "low speed" is used for a long time, the current will be too large and the electronic components in the battery box will be broken down. â€¢ (Optional) How to use constant speed cruise: When going straight, operate the "1" rocker, and at the same time, toggle the "4" switch, release the "1" rocker, the machine will always move forward or backward, and toggle the "4" switch again , the cruise control function is canceled. ( When turning, please be sure to cancel the cruise control function ) *Introduction to the remote start and flameout function of the remote control: When using the remote control to start, turn on the "main power switch", turn on the "power switch", turn on the "start key", increase the "throttle", and move "6" to "outward". key (about 3 seconds), the engine starts, and after starting, the "6" key returns to the center; push the "6" key "inward" (about 3 seconds), until the engine is turned off, and the "6" key returns to the center.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>HS800  lawn mower</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>HS800  lawn mower</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
